 ;; ── Regulation behind a constant that is compiled into this service ──────────
 ;;
 ;; This is the part of the catalog that is load-bearing rather than descriptive.
 ;; :threshold/code-path and :threshold/code-symbol name a literal in the source
 ;; tree; the verifier reads that literal and fails when it and :threshold/value
 ;; disagree. Changing the fallback threshold without moving the citation, or
 ;; citing a rule that no longer says this number, both break the build.
 :thresholds
 [{:threshold/id :ctr-usd
   :threshold/value 10000
   :threshold/currency "USD"
   :threshold/comparison :strictly-greater-than
   :threshold/code-path "app/api/screen/transaction/route.ts"
   :threshold/code-symbol "DEFAULT_TRANSACTION_THRESHOLD_USD"
   :threshold/authority "Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN), 31 CFR 1010.311"
   :threshold/source-url "https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-01-01/title-31.xml?section=1010.311&subtitle=B&chapter=X&part=1010&subpart=C"
   :threshold/human-url "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-31/subtitle-B/chapter-X/part-1010/subpart-C/section-1010.311"
   :source/http-status 200
   :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-21T02:34:46Z"
   :threshold/quoted-text
   "Each financial institution other than a casino shall file a report of each deposit, withdrawal, exchange of currency or other payment or transfer, by, through, or to such financial institution which involves a transaction in currency of more than $10,000, except as otherwise provided in this section."
   :threshold/note
   "The regulation says 'more than $10,000', so the code comparison is > and not >=. The eCFR versioner URL is pinned to the 2026-01-01 edition, which is why the quoted text is reproducible; :threshold/human-url tracks the current edition and may drift from it."}]

